# double:
# A natural added to itself: the fold over n from n by successor. Its scheme
# nat_type -> nat_type is the lemma double_scheme of native_arithmetic.pl.
. (λtuple. tuple λn. nat_fold n successor n)
λ double
# even:
# Whether a natural is even: true at zero, and the negation at each
# successor. Its scheme nat_type -> boolean_type is the lemma even_scheme of
# native_arithmetic.pl. The step is the negation written out, with no
# filter, so that the reference evaluator reads the fold in time linear in
# the natural: boolean_not filters its results by boolean_type, and the
# reference reads both sides of each filter, about three times the work at
# each step (measured 2026-10-28: boolean_not applied 4, 6
# and 8 times to true takes 28,157, 245,302 and 2,195,253 inferences).
. (λtuple. tuple λn. nat_fold true (λb. b false true) n)
